            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<h3><strong>Invisible Stressors Hiding in Plain Sight</strong></h3><h5><em>Indoor Air Pollutants</em></h5><p>Dust, pollen, smoke, VOCs (volatile organic componds), pet dander, and even cooking fumes can build<br/>up in your home’s air. Over time, breathing in these pollutants can cause<br/>allergy flare-ups, affect concentration, and reduce sleep quality.  </p><h5><em>Electromagnetic & Noise Clutter</em></h5><p>From the constant presence of Wi-Fi and devices to the low hum of appliances, unseen tech exposure and subtle noise may leave your nervous system in a state of low-level stress.</p><h5><em>Poor Lighting & Airflow</em></h5><p>Dim, artificial lighting and stale, stagnant air can make you feel sluggish and interfere with your natural wake-sleep rhythm.</p><h5><em>Chemical Overload</em></h5><p>Cleaning products, synthetic fragrances, and off-gassing from new furniture or flooring release irritants that can linger in the air and affect your long-term health.</p><p> </p><h3><strong>Home Wellness Reset: Fixing Invisible Stressors Holistically</strong></h3><h3></h3><p>Building a healthier home starts from layering small,<br/>impactful changes that address different types of stressors.</p><h5><em>Air Wellness — Purify and Refresh</em></h5><p>An air purifier can help remove pollutants, allergens, and odors, creating a cleaner breathing environment. Today’s leading air wellness solutions combine powerful filtration with design that complements your home in style and comfort or wellbeing.</p><h5><em>Natural Rhythm and Light</em></h5><p>Maximize natural light<br/>during the day and use warm, dim lighting in the evening to support your<br/>circadian rhythm. Open windows when possible, to circulate fresh air.</p><h5><em>Noise Mindfulness</em></h5><p>Soft furnishings like rugs, curtains, and upholstered furniture can help absorb sound. Consider adding white-noise machines or calming playlists to mask disruptive background sounds.</p><h5><em>Green, Clean Living</em></h5><p>Switch to non-toxic, fragrance-free cleaning products and choose low-VOC plants to naturally improve air quality. Always ventilate when using any products with strong scents or<br/>chemicals.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
